  "term": "mAChR",
  "definition": "mAChR is a receptor through which acetylcholine, or the similar compound carbachol, can trigger intracellular signaling. In the supplied source, activation of mAChR in enterochromaffin cells starts an IP3-related calcium pathway that helps promote serotonin (5-HT) release.",
